{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating action commits from perception states. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, directed recovery. Recovery states allow only one turn direction and never allow forward or random_walk. full_rotate is reserved for repeated or dead-end obstacles. All uncontrollable events are total and transitions are deterministic.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion-perception interface and specification for safe, coverage-biased exploration.",
    "Use helper commit and recovery states to ensure one-shot actions and safe transitions after obstacles, with random_walk as the main exploration action in clear."
  ],
